            <div xml:id="d1570">

                <pb facs="1000" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/40.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Chargé O’Shaughnessy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-10T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 10, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 720, January 9th. Navy Department has sent appropriate instructions to
                    Admiral Cowles regarding situation at Tepic.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
